# 02_researcher.kzp -- the hand-entered records (tier researcher) and the issue texts of profile
# c1-bp-b051eb0.
#
# A researcher record stands for a modelling choice no cited text states by itself; it never decides a
# status (it cannot be caller-side, QT-4/QT-9) and never justifies taking a call context out of a
# readiness specification (the checker requires a cited source for that).  The issue records quote only a
# few words; the full texts are in cases/C1.md (F1, F6).
phi 1;

prov r_axiom_program_order {
  tier researcher;
  kind researcher;
  authored "2026-10-24, C1 profile, from SPEC_FINAL 1.9 and 3.16 row R1 (as cfs-v7.0.1); cases inspected: C1";
  note "Program order inside one actor is an axiom of the model (A3, A4), not a cited text.";
}

prov r_countsem_by_name {
  tier researcher;
  kind researcher;
  authored "2026-10-24, C1 profile, from plan/C1_basis_plan.md 1.2 and 9.1; cases inspected: C1";
  note "The counting semaphore is keyed by its name: the lookup compares names (OS_ObjectIdFindByName). Two states: ABSENT, LIVE. The RESERVED window inside OS_CountSemCreate (name visible before the id is final) is not modelled: it is the follow-up item A5 of P-C1HOLD, outside C1. No application of the closure calls OS_CountSemDelete (plan/C1_build_manifest.md 8.5, the countsem API callers); it is reached from the cleanup of an application's resources (CFE_ES_CleanupObjectCallback) and from OS_DeleteAllObjects at teardown (OS_CleanUpObject). Since 2026-10-24 the delete is an effect (OS_CountSemDelete.retire) whose name the record does not give: from such an event on the kind is not fixed by the record. A name is not re-created in this subset; where a delete may lie between two attempts the attempts are not counted as one loop (the generation boundary of the retry monitor).";
}

prov r_countsem_type_slices {
  tier researcher;
  kind researcher;
  authored "2026-10-24, C1 profile, from the cited OSAL code (osal_* records of 01_prov.kzp) and the static closure plan/C1_build_manifest.md 8.5; cases inspected: C1";
  note "Key separation of the OSAL object table for osal.countsem (the 'via' of the bindings in 10_kinds.kzp). OS_common_record_t and the per-type internal records are shared by every object type, so the static closure lists writers of every type. A counting semaphore record lies in the slice at OS_COUNTSEM_BASE (osal_countsem_slice), and the shared helpers address a record only through a token of one object type (osal_find_next_free, osal_find_next_match). active_id and name_entry are written by OS_ObjectIdInit (whole table), by OS_ObjectIdFindNextFree, OS_ObjectIdConvertToken in EXCLUSIVE mode and OS_ObjectIdTransactionFinish with a final id or in EXCLUSIVE mode (osal_convert_token_exclusive, osal_convert_token_restore, osal_transaction_finish), and by the OS_OBJECT_INIT of a create; obj_name by OS_CountSemAPI_Init and OS_CountSemCreate. A countsem-typed token in a mode that writes is made only by OS_CountSemCreate (OS_ObjectIdAllocateNew(LOCAL_OBJID_TYPE), osapi-countsem.c 94, EXCLUSIVE, osal_allocate_new) and OS_CountSemDelete (EXCLUSIVE, osapi-countsem.c 123); Give, Take, TimedWait use lock mode NONE and GetInfo GLOBAL without a final id (osal_countsem_lock_none, osal_countsem_getinfo). Every other EXCLUSIVE token of the closure's OSAL is of another type: OS_ObjectIdAllocateNew at osapi-condvar.c 90, osapi-task.c 182, osapi-binsem.c 102, osapi-mutex.c 99, osapi-printf.c 95, osapi-queue.c 98, osapi-timebase.c 122, osapi-time.c 134, osapi-sockets.c 129 and 252, osapi-dir.c 119, osapi-module.c 203, osapi-filesys.c 153 and 274, osapi-file.c 136; OS_ObjectIdGetById(EXCLUSIVE) at osapi-condvar.c 119, osapi-task.c 219, osapi-binsem.c 131, osapi-mutex.c 128, osapi-queue.c 130, osapi-timebase.c 231, osapi-time.c 387, osapi-sockets.c 165 and 301, osapi-dir.c 150, osapi-module.c 271, osapi-file.c 167; OS_ObjectIdGetByName(EXCLUSIVE) at osapi-filesys.c 360 (each with its own type; grep of the pinned OSAL, the same in both bundle candidates). Hence a write changes osal.countsem only inside OS_ObjectIdInit, OS_CountSemAPI_Init, OS_CountSemCreate or OS_CountSemDelete (SPEC 4.2 step 8, NO_KEY by distinct type constants); the effects of those four operations stand for their writes. Not shown here: indirect calls (the adapter does not separate a writer whose function is an indirect-call target), and the RESERVED window (A5).";
}

prov r_reads_from_lookup {
  tier researcher;
  kind researcher;
  authored "2026-10-24, C1 profile, from SPEC_FINAL 3.16 row RF and 3.17 'Outcome-implied reads-from'; cases inspected: C1";
  note "A successful OS_CountSemGetIdByName returns the active_id of the record whose name matched (osal_find_by_name, osal_find_next_match); that id was written into the record by the OS_ObjectIdFinalizeNew of its creation, which also returned it through the creator's out-parameter (osal_finalize_new); a later object in the same slot has another id (osal_find_next_free). So a lookup whose out id equals the id a recorded creation returned read from that creation (the same generation): the reads-from edge of rule RF (stratum O, observed synchronization). The edge rests on the success outcome and on the equality of the two recorded ids; it gives no order for a failed lookup (an order the outcome alone decides, SPEC 4.8 'Trace analysis' step 4, 'outcome-decided').";
}

prov r_role_binding {
  tier researcher;
  kind researcher;
  authored "2026-10-24, C1 profile, from SPEC rev 1.3 amendment 1.6 Call contexts and plan/C1_basis_plan.md 9.7; cases inspected: C1";
  note "A role binds a call context to a declared site: the site event follows the return of the call on the same actor (an after-call probe in the caller). The binding of a site to a binary (a function of a release build, inlining) is stated in the observation plan, not here.";
}

prov issue_184_body {
  tier issue-derived;
  kind issue;
  side caller;
  cite "nasa/CF issue #184, body (2022-01-13): the CF app expects that semaphore to be created before it starts";
  note "Written about 2a024d8 (cases/C1.md F1); cited for the role of CF's lookup (a dependent use), not as an Allowed entry.";
}
